The predictor is normalized at each step, the likelihood product is exact, and the alternative code handles every sequence with an explicit branch flag. The first-symbol lower bound is for some alphabet symbol, not every symbol. No arbitrary iid alphabet lower bound is silently transferred to the stochastic-block-model family.
\paragraph{Audit corrections.} The alphabet obstruction is separated from the graph-model target. Ideal log loss, actual prefix-code length, and unavoidable model-identification cost are not conflated.
\paragraph{External computation.} None; symbolic arguments and boundary checks only.
